                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "So there are 6 mini-games.  The mini-games were of varying quality.  I only liked the hospital wave shooter.\n\n1) Mini-arcade basketball - not much here, just make as many baskets as you can within the time limit.  Pretty basic and pretty boring.  There are leaderboards.\n\n2) Light saber - You can either melee or block bullets with your light saber (and ricochet them back) or dodge, 180 degrees in front of you.  It's interesting the first time you play this, but then you notice the lack of depth here.  There's really no reason to play more than once. \n\n3) Bow shooting wave shooter.  The bow doesn't feel right.  Enemies are 360 around you.  There are different \"types\" but they are pretty bland.  I've played maybe 20 different bow games in VR and this would be in the bottom 5 of my list.\n\n4) Hospital wave shooter.  One environment.  It's dark.  You have flashlight in one hand and a gun in the other.  This game is actually a lot of fun.  If there's one reason to buy Super VR Trainer it's for this mini-game.  It's like a simplified Brookhaven Experiment, more arcade style.  The graphics are the best in this mini-game. Gun play is suprisingly effective.  Good atmosphere.  \n\n5) Hoverboard.  It's really an endless runner.  Looks a lot like Race the Sun.  However, the controls are terrible.  Honestly, you get bored quick here.\n\n6) Puzzle game.  Looked decent.  However, no tutorial and no explanation on how to progress.  I matched colors and it didn't seem to have any effect.  Not sure if it was a bug or if I misunderstood the rules (which I didn't find).\n\nSo was this game worth $3.59?  I'm not sure.  I don't think I'd want to play any of the mini-games again, except for the hospital wave shooter.  So is $3.59 worth that one mini-game when it only has 1 environment and 1 gun?  I don't think I can justify the price.  It definitely is noth worth $17.99 either.  \n\nSale Price Rating 4/10, Normal Price Rating 2/10 Just play rec room, it has better mini-games and it's free",
